cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: pysrat
abstract: >-
  A Python package for fitting and analysing NHPP (non-homogeneous Poisson
  process) software reliability models. It provides a scikit-learn-style API
  and EM algorithm implementations in C++ exposed via pybind11, together with
  multi-factor (metrics-based) models in which the fault-detection probability
  is described by a generalized linear model. Logit, probit and cloglog links
  are built in, an offset term expresses Cox proportional-hazards models, and
  user-defined link functions can be added by supplying the inverse link and
  its derivative.
